# Local upload inbox credentials. Copy to `.env` and fill in real values.
# `.env` is gitignored — never commit tokens or private hosts.
#
# This file is OPTIONAL.
#
# The address of the inbox is learned at runtime, so a board that was flashed
# once works with the inbox of whoever is holding it. Run the inbox on your
# machine and point the board at it:
#
#   python mosaico.py iris rpc 0x1002 1 \
#       --payload "http://your-laptop.local:8765" \
#       --project .
#
# The board keeps the address in NVS, so it survives a restart and a
# firmware update.
#
# Fill this file in only for a private inbox that the board cannot find by
# itself, for example one behind a tunnel:
#
#   UPLOAD_ORIGIN=https://your-private-inbox      the fallback for a board
#                                                    that learned nothing
#   UPLOAD_TOKEN=<64-hex-chars-from-your-inbox>   the token for that inbox
#
# The name in UPLOAD_ORIGIN may be a name or an address. A name that ends in
# .local is resolved by the board with a multicast mDNS query, so it follows
# the machine and the address of the machine may change under it. The inbox
# prints the line to copy.
#
# The origin is read when the build is configured, not when it compiles. A
# changed .env needs the configure step to run again, otherwise the old
# origin stays in the firmware:
#
#   rm -rf build && python3 .../idf_low_noise_build.py --project ... build
